  'honest_assessment': 'Vardhman is the benchmark supplier for combed cotton yarn and woven fabric in India - if you need consistent 40s, 60s, or 80s count combed yarn in large volumes, they are the first call.

Their yarn quality consistency is genuinely exceptional - lot-to-lot CV% is among the lowest in the industry, which matters enormously for downstream knitters and weavers who cant afford shade variation. The Mahavir Spinning division produces some of the finest compact spun yarn available domestically.

That said, Vardhman is not a flexible supplier. Their minimum order for yarn is typically 1 tonne per count per shade, and their fabric minimum is 3,000 metres per design. Small garment exporters or boutique fashion brands will get poor attention - they are geared for volume customers.

Lead times for dyed yarn are 4-6 weeks. Grey fabric is quicker at 2-3 weeks. Payment terms are strictly 30 days for new buyers - no credit until 6+ months relationship.

Pricing is 8-12% above smaller Tirupur or Ichalkaranji mills but the quality premium is justified for export-quality end products where rejection rates matter.',
